     "body": "### magpie version\n\n0.1.4196\n\n### Where\n\nGUI\n\n### OS\n\nmacOS 15.6.1 (darwin/arm64)\n\n### Agent, provider and model\n\nClaude Code → Antigravity (plugin `@magpie-community/opencode-antigravity-auth` 0.1.16) → Gemini 4 Hydrogen\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Sign in to Antigravity with a Google AI Pro account (plugin provider, not the built-in one), User-Agent `antigravity/hub/2.32.1`.\n2. Refresh the model list: `magpie provider models antigravity` reports **11 models** — `gemini-3.8-flash`, `claude-sonnet-4-6`, `claude-opus-4-6-thinking`, `gpt-oss-120b-medium`, `gemini-2.5-flash`, `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`, `gemini-3-flash`, `gemini-3.1-flash-image`, `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `gemini-3.5-flash-lite`, `gemini-3.8-flash-tiered`. No `gemini-4-*` at all, so Gemini 4 Hydrogen cannot be picked from the catalog.\n3. Expose it anyway: `magpie provider models antigravity +\"Gemini 4 Hydrogen\"`.\n4. In Claude Code, `/model` → `Gemini 4 Hydrogen · Antigravity`, then send any message.\n\n### What happened, and what you expected\n\n**What happened:** every turn fails with HTTP 404:\n\n```text\nThere's an issue with the selected model (antigravity/Gemini 4 Hydrogen[1m]).\nIt may not exist or you may not have access to it.\n```\n\nThe routing log shows the pick is sent to the plugin as the display name, not as an Antigravity id:\n\n```text\nmodel=antigravity/Gemini 4 Hydrogen\ntry.model=Gemini 4 Hydrogen\nsentBy=plugin\nstatus=404\nerror=Antigravity: model Gemini 4 Hydrogen not found\n```\n\nBecause `Gemini 4 Hydrogen` is not in the live Antigravity catalog, `AntigravityVariants` returns `ok=false` and the string goes upstream unchanged; the upstream 404 turns into `model ... not found`.\n\n**What I expected:** on a Google AI Pro account, Antigravity should list its Gemini 4 models (`gemini-4-hydrogen`, `gemini-4-argon`) the way other reports show (#6596 lists them for Antigravity, #5679 shows a Windows/2.29.0 install getting 26 models / 20 kept where a stale macOS install got 23 / 17 and Gemini 4 Argon 404'd). The same Google account serves `models/gemini-4-hydrogen` through the `google` provider without problems, so the entitlement exists.\n\nTwo separable problems, I don't know which is the cause:\n\n1. **The catalog fetch is missing the Gemini 4 family** even though the list is freshly fetched and the plugin sends the current Hub UA. A 11-model list looks smaller than the 20+ other users report. Could the plugin stop at the first entitlement tier that `fetchAvailableModels` accepts and never ask the higher one?\n2. **A model that is not in the catalog is forwarded verbatim**, so adding a model by display name turns into a permanent 404 instead of an error at pick time (\"not offered by this account\"). If (1) is expected behavior, this is at least worth a clearer failure.\n\nRelated: #5679 (macOS stale Hub UA → fewer models → Gemini 4 Argon 404), #3617 (bare family id reaching upstream → 404), #3027 (`gemini-4-argon-disabled`).\n\n### Error text or logs\n\n`magpie provider models antigravity`:\n\n```text\n✓ 11 models from antigravity\n  Antigravity  antigravity\n  billing    plan\n  account    <redacted>  Google AI Pro  from antigravity's own sign-in\n  models     1 exposed of 11 from antigravity · fetched just now\n             antigravity/Gemini 4 Hydrogen\n  used by    Claude Code\n```\n\nRouting log (routing/2026-11-14.jsonl):\n\n```json\n{\"time\":\"2026-11-14T10:52:40.200153-08:00\",\"agent\":\"claude\",\"session\":\"…\",\"model\":\"antigravity/Gemini 4 Hydrogen\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"provider\":\"antigravity\",\"order\":[{\"id\":\"antigravity\",\"provider\":\"antigravity\",\"name\":\"Antigravity\",\"kind\":\"account\",\"plan\":\"Google AI Pro\",\"model\":\"Gemini 4 Hydrogen\"}],\"tries\":[{\"id\":\"antigravity\",\"model\":\"Gemini 4 Hydrogen\",\"start\":\"2026-11-14T10:52:40.208886-08:00\",\"done\":true,\"status\":404,\"ms\":2379,\"sentBy\":\"plugin\",\"fail\":\"other\",\"error\":\"Antigravity: model Gemini 4 Hydrogen not found\"}],\"done\":true,\"status\":404,\"error\":\"Antigravity: model Gemini 4 Hydrogen not found\"}\n```\n",
